  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a disturbing historical photograph of emaciated individuals, likely Holocaust victims, in a state of extreme suffering and death, juxtaposed with the text 'this project is tough but it will save the world.' The visual material is mapped onto the textual material via analogy: the suffering and death of victims are used to metaphorically represent a 'tough project' that will 'save the world.' This is harmful because it trivializes the immense human suffering and genocide depicted in the image by reducing it to a motivational or aspirational cliché. The meme uses the image of extreme human suffering to justify or frame a difficult endeavor as noble or necessary, which can be seen as exploitative and disrespectful to the victims. The intent is to evoke a sense of urgency or moral justification for a project by invoking the gravity of historical atrocity, potentially normalizing or minimizing the horror of the depicted event. The overall intent is harmful as it risks desensitizing viewers to the gravity of historical trauma and may be used to justify or legitimize difficult or ethically ambiguous projects by association with suffering.",
